  "requests": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/notes/d8a48318-c5e6-4983-b3d3-2f53239226b0/blocks",
      "status": 201,
      "body": {
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "plain_text": "POWER SERIES — A working definition. A power series is a sum of powers centred at a fixed point. Its interval of convergence describes where the series settles to a finite value."
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/notes/d8a48318-c5e6-4983-b3d3-2f53239226b0/blocks",
      "status": 201,
      "body": {
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "plain_text": "Inside the radius, the series converges absolutely. Outside it, the terms cannot settle. Check each endpoint separately."
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/notes/d8a48318-c5e6-4983-b3d3-2f53239226b0/blocks",
      "status": 201,
      "body": {
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "plain_text": "THE CHAMPION PRINCIPLE — Find the term that governs the limit. Divide by that term, then let the smaller contributions disappear."
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/api/notes/d8a48318-c5e6-4983-b3d3-2f53239226b0/blocks",
      "status": 201,
      "body": {
        "block_type": "paragraph",
        "plain_text": "A useful question: what remains unchanged when the representation changes? The content and its coordinates stay fixed while the paper takes on a different material."
      }
    },
    {
